window.docContents[8].resolve({"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--The-Interaction-Algebra-_LPAR_Flater-Appendix-C_RPAR_--The-ternary-product-of-kinds-_LPAR_Flater-App___-C_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\n holds when kind  times kind  yields\nkind . It is partial and curated: an application asserts the legitimate\nproducts of its kinds, each carrying the dimensional\ncoherence obligation discharged by the homomorphism theorem.\n\nRealized as the KMul field of InteractionAlgebra: a ternary relation over\ndimensioned kinds, paired in the same structure with the\nwell-formedness field kMul_coherent that requires every edge to satisfy\n. The structure cannot be formed for an\nalgebra that violates coherence.\n\n is the division dual of the kind product:  divided by  yields . Fuel-consumption \nrainfall is the classic Flater example whose careless handling yields a category\nerror rather than a number.\n\nRealized as InteractionAlgebra.KDiv, defined as the product read backwards\n(), so it inherits the same\npartiality and coherence side-condition.\n\nMultiplication and division are inverse on kinds. A product and its quotient\nhold together — the round-trip is an equivalence:\n\nTogether with dimensional coherence this is the\ncalculus that OWL2 cannot host: an algebraic law with arithmetic side-conditions,\nproved rather than consistency-checked. Builds on the kind product and the kind quotient.\n\nImmediate from defining KDiv as the converse of KMul: the biconditional is\nIff.rfl. The round-trip is the symmetry of that definition.\n\nWorked instance. Torque times plane angle is energy, and energy is not torque,\neven though . Formally\n holds while\n — the small example that shows the algebra\ncarrying information dimension alone discards. Uses the kind product.\n\nProved in the Interaction module. torque, angle (dimension one), and\nenergy are declared as dimensioned kinds, with torque and energy both given\ndimension force · length; the product edge torque_angle_energy is asserted in\nthe worked siMech algebra and its coherence checked by the Dimension-group\ncomputation, while energy.kind ≠ torque.kind is by decide.\n\n","context":"PropertyKindCalculus Blueprint\u0009The Interaction Algebra (Flater Appendix C)","header":"10.1. The ternary product of kinds (Flater App. C)","id":"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--The-Interaction-Algebra-_LPAR_Flater-Appendix-C_RPAR_--The-ternary-product-of-kinds-_LPAR_Flater-App___-C_RPAR_"}});